summary:
  The level poll stays at full rate in a window the listener has left for another.

history:
  A window stays up beside other work for a day. The listener clicks a
  station and goes back to typing in another window: the pointer is still
  on the player. With the pointer alone as the sign, that was a shell
  asking the sound server every two seconds for as long as the typing
  lasted, and a window minimised from the keyboard kept its last "the
  pointer is here" for good. In a window it takes the pointer and the
  keyboard.

target:
  package/contents/ui/WindowLogic.js

find:
      if (seat === "window") return hovered === true && active === true;

replace:
      if (seat === "window") return hovered === true;

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_windowlogic.qml::test_in_the_window_it_takes_the_pointer_and_the_keyboard.
